WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.433
- There's a lot of beans in there

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:02.732
I hope you sleep by yourself.

00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:04.666
Ba-ba-ba-ba-ba!
(laughter)

00:00:05.878 --> 00:00:07.568
(drums playing)

00:00:09.674 --> 00:00:11.498
- My mom is from like
a really small village

00:00:11.498 --> 00:00:15.155
in Tobago which is like the
sister island of Trinidad.

00:00:15.155 --> 00:00:15.977
- Yeah.

00:00:15.977 --> 00:00:17.394
- Each village has their own harvest so

00:00:17.394 --> 00:00:20.018
around harvest time Black
Cake is always coming out.

00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:23.059
- This my friends is a
very very very very very

00:00:23.059 --> 00:00:25.416
popular dish called
Tembleque, all I'd eat was

00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:28.949
frijol negro which is like black
beans with rice and tostone

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:31.168
and Tembleque, like that was like my diet

00:00:31.168 --> 00:00:32.916
whenever I went to Puerto Rico.

00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:34.569
- My family would get
together on the weekends

00:00:34.569 --> 00:00:36.600
and there was this lady like up in 181st

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.783
you'll see like a long
line in New York City

00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:41.430
there's people waiting to
buy the Habichuelas con dulce

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.042
- My father he does a lot of poetry

00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:46.481
and we go to like African
and Caribbean festivals

00:00:46.481 --> 00:00:48.721
and we'd go and buy these from the

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:49.858
street vendors.

00:00:49.858 --> 00:00:51.448
- My first introduction to Pain Patate was

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:53.202
probably during my communion because it

00:00:53.202 --> 00:00:55.720
so hefty sometimes it would
literally be the only meal

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.149
it's like what are you in the mood for

00:00:57.149 --> 00:00:58.808
oh today Pain Patate and then they

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:00.086
would just make that and then that's

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:01.166
what you would have for dinner.

00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:02.664
- This is like the most
Cuban thing I've ever said

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:06.621
My tia Yoya would take the bus and visit

00:01:06.621 --> 00:01:08.502
my grandfather, my
grandfather's sister, and she

00:01:08.502 --> 00:01:10.696
always made flan for us, when it was time

00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:12.844
to see Tia Yoya, it was
time to eat some flan.

00:01:12.844 --> 00:01:14.958
Even though flan is very popular in other

00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:17.198
countries if I didn't choose this I would

00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:19.066
be disowned by my own people.

00:01:19.066 --> 00:01:20.233
I love you!

00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:21.784
- You ready?

00:01:21.784 --> 00:01:22.723
- I'm ready let's do this.

00:01:22.723 --> 00:01:23.883
- Yo you ain't ready for this!

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.992
- Don't drop it I swear to God

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.268
- I got this.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.363
- Cookies are awesome, they
have the cross in there

00:01:30.363 --> 00:01:31.616
- Those cookies came straight from

00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:32.939
the Dominican Republic, alright?

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:34.182
So you enjoy every cookie.

00:01:34.182 --> 00:01:35.906
- That's really good.

00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:40.089
- It feels like the yam was soaked

00:01:40.089 --> 00:01:41.448
in there for so long, it's really sweet.

00:01:41.448 --> 00:01:42.911
Let me dip it in the beans actually.

00:01:42.911 --> 00:01:44.026
- That's a good idea.

00:01:44.026 --> 00:01:45.912
You've discovered something new.

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:50.225
- Open up like a Jamaican
Dominican fusion treat store.

00:01:50.225 --> 00:01:51.577
- Oh my God.

00:01:51.606 --> 00:01:52.188
(laughter)

00:01:52.188 --> 00:01:53.789
- We're gonna be rich, okay we gotta cut

00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:55.815
this is our idea.
(laughter)

00:01:56.006 --> 00:01:56.680
- Cheers.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:57.893
- La Haim.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.719
- Yeah great, it's coconut-y but it's not.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:01.579
- It's subtle.

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:02.948
I did a good job when I made it.

00:02:02.948 --> 00:02:04.283
That's so funny you don't like coconut

00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:05.718
I don't like raisins.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.663
- Tell me what you taste.

00:02:06.663 --> 00:02:08.125
- It's so good it's almost
like a bread pudding.

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:09.485
It doesn't feel unhealthy.

00:02:09.485 --> 00:02:10.785
- Wow you should tell my Mom that.

00:02:10.785 --> 00:02:12.062
- I'm so impressed with this, I could eat

00:02:12.062 --> 00:02:13.559
this all the time, thank you so much.

00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:15.125
It's so good, thank you.

00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:16.206
- [Mother on Phone] You're welcome.

00:02:16.206 --> 00:02:17.227
- I like her so much.

00:02:17.227 --> 00:02:18.086
- My mom is dope.

00:02:18.086 --> 00:02:19.620
- It dances, even the flan knows

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.523
how to dance meringue, bom-ba-dom-ba-dom

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:22.499
- Check this out.

00:02:22.499 --> 00:02:24.037
- It's really good.

00:02:24.565 --> 00:02:25.458
- I know, I know my shit.

00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:26.944
I'm gonna dive into this flan, this looks

00:02:26.944 --> 00:02:29.273
like an enemy from Final Fantasy 7.

00:02:29.359 --> 00:02:31.217
That is bomb, that is very good.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.423
- Yeah it looks like there's hair in it

00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:34.618
I didn't realize that it was
because of the sweet potato.

00:02:34.618 --> 00:02:36.185
Considering that I've
been eating sweet potato

00:02:36.185 --> 00:02:37.925
every day like a good girl.

00:02:37.925 --> 00:02:39.203
- Why?

00:02:39.203 --> 00:02:41.119
- It's packed with nutrients, this is not

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:43.800
an after school special, what is happening

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.682
right now we are crossing the streams.

00:02:48.582 --> 00:02:50.011
- The funny thing about
the Caribbean is like

00:02:50.011 --> 00:02:52.797
you pretty much like remixes of each other

00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:54.295
- I was raised in the Bronx you know

00:02:54.295 --> 00:02:55.875
there's like Dominicans,
Puerto Ricans, but

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.290
this is awesome and I actually want

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.113
to like look up the recipe and make it.

00:02:59.113 --> 00:03:02.051
- It's crazy that I visited your country

00:03:02.051 --> 00:03:04.475
but did not have your country's food

00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:06.113
and I am missing out clearly.

00:03:06.113 --> 00:03:08.016
- I feel like at home, having you eat

00:03:08.016 --> 00:03:10.327
that Tembleque, like my heart is happy.

00:03:10.327 --> 00:03:11.477
- And my mom is happy.

00:03:11.477 --> 00:03:12.429
- Yes.

00:03:12.429 --> 00:03:14.692
- That you at some Black
Cake from Trinidad.

00:03:14.692 --> 00:03:16.492
- You know I live by
Jamaicans in New York City

00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:18.628
and I never ever tasted this, I'm glad

00:03:18.628 --> 00:03:20.914
I was able to taste
this, this is delicious

00:03:20.914 --> 00:03:21.913
this is amazing.

00:03:21.913 --> 00:03:23.051
- Shout out to the Cubans, this is bomb.

00:03:23.051 --> 00:03:24.381
- Shout out to the Haitians.

00:03:24.897 --> 00:03:26.364
(laughter)

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.577
- Crazy man.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.084
(laughter)

